Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||05-09-2001||03:03 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48183907&Sequence=0&res=high">  <P>Almost ready for the upcoming season of autocrossing. Over the weekend I got the car out , changed the oil , Fixed a relay that was causing the car to crank over a lot before starting and washed the car. I still need to get my new Pirelli's put on the back and finish my Brake upgrade. I drove the car around the block a few times with no dash in it (still puttin in my white gauge faces) and it seemed to run great.<P>Still need to fix a few things , want to get the windows tinted as soon as I get the car on the road permanently. You will notice from the pic that the car sits really low , I found that a pop can will NOT fit under the side of the car. But does it ever corner! Stil need my front mount battery, and a few other little things.<P>I'm wondering if anyone has ever replaced a gas pedal? My pedal broke and I would just as soon replace the pedal and arm , rather than try to replace the pedal itseolf. Can anyone lend me some advice??<P>Thanks<P>Jonathan M. McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>17" TR motorsports Typhoons<BR>225/45/17 Front<BR>255/40/17" rear<BR>11.25" vented Discs (all 4 corners)<BR>Wilwood 4 piston Dynalite 2 calipers up front<BR>Braided brake lines<BR>Short shift<BR>Cold air<BR>Koni's all around<BR>Ground control coil overs<BR>Ultimate dog bone<BR>Big sway bars front & Rear<BR>no cat<BR>Geni Stailness steel exhaust tips<BR>Blocked EGR<BR>White face gauges<BR>Pioneer DEH6000CD<BR>Sony Mobile 4x50 amp<BR>Momo pedals & shifter<BR>Front mount battery (IP)(in progress)<BR>42,000 original miles<BR>Shown , Tracked , Autocrossed , Abused...<BR>Waiting for N* ....<P>Oh yeah , the windshield decal says Grassroots motorsports.com a autocross/ Scca magazine.<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 05-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||05-09-2001||03:10 PM||||I don't know about the gas pedal but I am wondering about what relay you replaced.  Could you tell me which one and did it fix the problem?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||05-09-2001||03:15 PM||||Both the relays on the firewall were somewhat corroded , I removed the undertray of both vents to cool the engine better at track events where I would run between 4500 and 6000 for 20 min at a time. These relay's are located over the air canister ont he fire wall. I believe one relay is for oil pressure the other is the fuel pump relay. In anycase both were corroded so I cleaned them up a bit and the problem was gone, this was over a 4 day period , it never gave me any problems...usually it does every few starts , it will crank over and over..then fire when oil pressure is up<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000003||onfire||05-09-2001||03:17 PM||||How wide are the rear wheels and what's the offset? Also did you do anything else to get those wide tires under there? <P>Oh by the way very nice.<BR> <BR>p.s. you need to update your website.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-09-2001||03:22 PM||||Oh man that car is horrible! you really need to dispose of it properly, you can bring it to my place where it can be processed all ya need to do is fill out the little blue form that you got when you purchased the car. I have a courtesy (87 Subaru GL)car I can loan you until you get another gorgeo uhum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lookaround_1.gif"> ... I mean another car.<P>Thank You<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||05-09-2001||03:22 PM||||The rear wheels are 8" , I didn't do a thing , with struts and stock lowering springs , the wheels were rubbing on hard corners (sidewall flex) SO I switched to the ground control coilovers , this allowed me to grind down the strut collar so there is easily enough room for the tire to clear and not interfere under hard cornering.<P>As for the offset , not too sure , I will have to check with the guy I got them from and get back to you on that one<P>As for my webpage , I made it 4 years ago , when geocities was bought by yahoo something changed , I can't get back into it with my old passwords , I used the switchover option but still no luck. I would love to build a new site as that one was last updated 2 years ago or so.<P>JM||||reg||1
