Z||000020||Slammed Fiero||05-10-2001||02:29 PM||||Lets not Inflate Lisa's ego anymore (haha JK)<BR>As for the relay it's the one under one of the engine vents (there are 2) both had corroded terminals so I cleaned them and it seemed to solve the problem.<P>As for the paint , it's original ..so It would be kinda a waste to paint it. If anything when I do get the car painted a few years down the road I will get it all monochromatic like an 88<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000021||sqoach||05-10-2001||02:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>As for the paint , it's original ..so It would be kinda a waste to paint it. If anything when I do get the car painted a few years down the road I will get it all monochromatic like an 88<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ohhhhh....For some reason I was thinking the 86s had black ground f/x. I guess that's just on the SE's. I thought you had repainted it. It looks new! On second thought...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||11
