Z||000023||Taijiguy||05-10-2001||04:55 PM||||Hmmm.....I dunno...both ya'll may be in for a disappointing season, Eric and ChadMan could be competitive....and well, what I can do remains to be seen   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||grinthock||05-10-2001||06:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Lets not Inflate Lisa's ego anymore (haha JK)<BR>As for the relay it's the one under one of the engine vents (there are 2) both had corroded terminals so I cleaned them and it seemed to solve the problem.<P>As for the paint , it's original ..so It would be kinda a waste to paint it. If anything when I do get the car painted a few years down the road I will get it all monochromatic like an 88<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>To Clarify.....<P>There is a relay in PARALLEL with  the oil pressure sending unit.  The relay is fired by the ignition and turns on the fuel pump (turn to JUST on you will hear ZEEEEEEEE for a sec) if that relay dies (and it WILL because it's exposed to rain, it's in front of the AIR CAN) the oil pressure sender is used as a BACKUP relay... So when there is oil pressure the fuel pump will run... PROBLEM, if the oil is HOT you can't get up enough pressure to fire the relay so you need to let the car cool (had that problem), SO if you have to CRANK CRANK CRANK before she starts check that relay socket it's probably corrorded, and the cranking action brings up the pressure enough to fire the pump.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Slammed Fiero||05-10-2001||06:49 PM||||The car is lowered with coilovers in the rear and Carrera springs up front. As for being disappointed at shows , I'm far more into racing , If some of my friends knew I went to shows I would be branded a Buff Boy. My car looking good is only the result of me buying a 18,000 mile car (haha) Makes maintenance sooo much easier. Plus washing it every day.(haha)<P>As for the oil being hot causing the car not to start..I have yet to experience that one , I have run the car at or near to WOT for 1/2 hour on end on the track , it always starts back up. I usually do a 2 min cool down lap at both shannonville and mosport , but other than that I bring the car in and shut it down. It's when the car used to sit for a while is when it would crank over before starting, no problem though , it's all fixed.<P>I'm just pondering a held motorsports tubular front end...Not good when I have money , bills don't get paid , Fiero always gets something nice (haha) <P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
